% test: head_pair_integer_to_constant
% expected: fail (subtyping does not apply)
% description: Subtyping relaxes body-body variable pairs only (Definition
%   "Well-Typed Clause with Subtyping").  A head-head pair still requires dual
%   types, so copying an Integer input to a Constant output within the head is
%   rejected even though Integer <: Constant.  The supported route is a direct
%   body-body connection; positive twin:
%   positive/subtyping/integer_below_number_and_constant.glp.

procedure elem(Integer?, Constant).
elem(X, X?).
